LP.page({"id": "roadmap-ai-data-engineer", "section": "roadmaps", "title": "Roadmap: → AI Data Engineer", "level": "Intermediate", "minutes": 8, "tags": ["roadmap", "ai data engineer"], "body": "\nThe AI Data Engineer is a Data Engineer whose pipelines feed AI systems. So you build the full DE foundation first, then add the AI-specific data layer. Each phase links to the exact lessons to study.\n\n## Phase 1 — Become a solid Data Engineer first\nThis is non-negotiable: AI data work rests on strong data engineering.\n**Study now:** [The full Data Engineer roadmap](#/page/roadmap-data-engineer) → work it end to end before continuing here.\n\n## Phase 2 — Understand what AI/ML needs from data\nLearn how models consume data so you can shape it correctly.\n**Study now:** [What is AI vs ML vs GenAI vs LLM](#/page/ai-ml-dl-genai-llm) · [AI Data Engineer — the role in depth](#/page/role-ai-data-engineer)\n\n## Phase 3 — Embeddings & vector databases\nThe core new skill: turning text/images into vectors and serving them for search and RAG.\n**Study now:** [GenAI 1 — how LLMs work](#/page/genai-llm-basics) · [GenAI 2 — embeddings, RAG, vectors](#/page/genai-rag)\n\n## Phase 4 — Pipelines that feed AI\nReliable ingestion, transformation and orchestration — now aimed at features and training data.\n**Study now:** [ETL & ELT](#/page/etl-concepts) · [Spark / PySpark](#/page/spark-basics) · [Orchestration with Airflow](#/page/orchestration-airflow)\n\n## Phase 5 — Quality, drift & governance for AI\nModels fail silently on bad/changing data. Own that.\n**Study now:** [Data quality & governance](#/page/data-quality-governance) · [Warehouses & lakehouse](#/page/warehouse-basics)\n\n<div class=\"callout callout-tip\"><span class=\"cfor\"><\/span><div><span class=\"ctitle\">Extra (beyond this academy):<\/span> a feature store (Feast), experiment tracking (MLflow), and data versioning (DVC/lakeFS). Learn these once you've shipped a RAG or feature pipeline.<\/div><\/div>\n\n> **Next:** drill the [Interview Bank](#/interview) (filter role = AI Data Engineer) and [compare all roles](#/page/role-comparison-table).\n"});
LP.page({"id": "roadmap-llm-engineer", "section": "roadmaps", "title": "Roadmap: → LLM Engineer", "level": "Advanced", "minutes": 8, "tags": ["roadmap", "llm engineer"], "body": "\nThe LLM Engineer works on the models themselves — fine-tuning, serving, optimisation. It's the deepest specialisation, so build Python + data fluency first, then go deep on models.\n\n## Phase 1 — Strong Python foundation\nYou'll live in Python and PyTorch.\n**Study now:** [Python 1 — the basics](#/page/py-basics) · [Python 2 — pandas & data](#/page/py-data)\n\n## Phase 2 — Understand LLMs deeply\nTokens, context windows, the transformer, attention, temperature.\n**Study now:** [GenAI 1 — how LLMs work & prompting](#/page/genai-llm-basics)\n\n## Phase 3 — RAG, embeddings & vectors\nEven model specialists must know retrieval — it's how models meet real data.\n**Study now:** [GenAI 2 — embeddings, RAG, agents & fine-tuning](#/page/genai-rag)\n\n## Phase 4 — Fine-tuning (LoRA / QLoRA)\nTeach models new behaviour efficiently.\n**Study now:** [Fine-tuning section in GenAI 2](#/page/genai-rag) · [GenAI vs LLM Engineer — the role](#/page/role-genai-llm-engineer)\n\n## Phase 5 — Serving & optimisation\nRun models cheaply and fast in production.\n**Study now:** [System design: HLD vs LLD](#/page/hld-lld) · [CAP & distributed systems](#/page/cap-distributed)\n\n<div class=\"callout callout-warn\"><span class=\"cfor\"><\/span><div>This is the most maths/infra-heavy role. Topics beyond this academy you'll need: deep learning with <b>PyTorch<\/b>, the Hugging Face stack (<b>transformers + PEFT<\/b>), <b>GPUs<\/b>, quantization, <b>vLLM<\/b>, and distributed training (<b>Ray/DeepSpeed<\/b>). Most jobs today are actually GenAI-Engineer-level — go there first if unsure.<\/div><\/div>\n\n> **Next:** [Interview Bank](#/interview) (role = LLM Engineer) · [compare all roles](#/page/role-comparison-table).\n"});
LP.page({"id": "roadmap-ml-engineer", "section": "roadmaps", "title": "Roadmap: → ML Engineer", "level": "Intermediate", "minutes": 7, "tags": ["roadmap", "ml engineer"], "body": "\nThe ML Engineer puts machine-learning models into reliable production software — software engineering plus ML. Strong overlap with data engineering, so this academy covers a big chunk of it.\n\n## Phase 1 — Python + SQL fluency\n**Study now:** [Python 1](#/page/py-basics) · [Python 2 — pandas](#/page/py-data) · [SQL 1](#/page/sql-basics)\n\n## Phase 2 — Data foundations\nModels are only as good as their data pipelines.\n**Study now:** [The data lifecycle](#/page/data-lifecycle) · [ETL & ELT](#/page/etl-concepts)\n\n## Phase 3 — ML fundamentals\nUnderstand training, evaluation, and the AI landscape.\n**Study now:** [AI vs ML vs DL vs GenAI vs LLM](#/page/ai-ml-dl-genai-llm)\n\n## Phase 4 — Productionising models at scale\nServing, scaling, orchestration, and system design.\n**Study now:** [Spark / PySpark](#/page/spark-basics) · [Cloud for engineers](#/page/cloud-for-de) · [Orchestration](#/page/orchestration-airflow) · [HLD vs LLD](#/page/hld-lld)\n\n## Phase 5 — Reliability & data quality\n**Study now:** [Data quality & governance](#/page/data-quality-governance) · [ACID & transactions](#/page/acid-transactions)\n\n<div class=\"callout callout-tip\"><span class=\"cfor\"><\/span><div><span class=\"ctitle\">Extra (beyond this academy):<\/span> classical ML with scikit-learn, deep learning with PyTorch/TensorFlow, and MLOps tooling (Docker, Kubernetes, MLflow, model registries, CI/CD for models).<\/div><\/div>\n\n> **Next:** [Interview Bank](#/interview) (role = ML Engineer) · [compare all roles](#/page/role-comparison-table).\n"});
LP.page({"id": "roadmap-data-scientist", "section": "roadmaps", "title": "Roadmap: → Data Scientist", "level": "Intermediate", "minutes": 7, "tags": ["roadmap", "data scientist"], "body": "\nThe Data Scientist builds models to predict and find deep insight — heavier on statistics and experimentation. This academy is engineering-focused, but several core skills overlap, and we'll be honest about what to learn elsewhere.\n\n## Phase 1 — Maths & statistics foundation\nProbability, distributions, hypothesis testing, regression. *(Core to DS; study via a stats course.)*\n\n## Phase 2 — Python + pandas\n**Study now:** [Python 1 — the basics](#/page/py-basics) · [Python 2 — pandas & wrangling](#/page/py-data)\n\n## Phase 3 — SQL for analysis\nPulling and shaping data is daily work.\n**Study now:** [SQL 1 — querying](#/page/sql-basics) · [SQL 2 — windows & CTEs](#/page/sql-advanced)\n\n## Phase 4 — Machine learning & modelling\n**Study now:** [AI vs ML vs DL vs GenAI vs LLM](#/page/ai-ml-dl-genai-llm) — then go deeper with scikit-learn and modelling courses.\n\n## Phase 5 — Communicating insight & trustworthy data\n**Study now:** [Data quality & governance](#/page/data-quality-governance) — clean inputs make trustworthy conclusions.\n\n<div class=\"callout callout-note\"><span class=\"cfor\"><\/span><div>This academy specialises in <b>data & AI engineering<\/b>. For full Data Science depth, pair these lessons with dedicated statistics, scikit-learn, experiment-design, and visualisation resources. The Python + SQL + data-quality skills here transfer directly.<\/div><\/div>\n\n> **Next:** [compare all roles](#/page/role-comparison-table) · [Interview Bank](#/interview).\n"});
LP.page({"id": "roadmap-data-analyst", "section": "roadmaps", "title": "Roadmap: → Data Analyst", "level": "Beginner", "minutes": 6, "tags": ["roadmap", "data analyst"], "body": "\nThe Data Analyst explains what already happened using SQL, dashboards and charts. It's one of the most accessible entry points into the data world — and a great springboard toward Data Engineer later.\n\n## Phase 1 — Data & spreadsheet basics\nUnderstand what data is and get comfortable with Excel/Sheets.\n**Study now:** [What is data, really?](#/page/what-is-data) · [Databases & SQL (gentle intro)](#/page/what-is-database)\n\n## Phase 2 — SQL (your #1 skill)\nAnalysts live in SQL. Get strong here.\n**Study now:** [SQL 1 — query like a pro](#/page/sql-basics) · [SQL 2 — windows, CTEs & optimisation](#/page/sql-advanced)\n\n## Phase 3 — Dashboards & visualisation\nPower BI / Tableau / Looker. *(Practice with the free desktop tools.)*\n\n## Phase 4 — Business metrics & storytelling\nTurn numbers into decisions people act on. *(Learn KPIs, funnels, cohort analysis.)*\n\n## Phase 5 — (Optional) level up to Data Engineer\nIf you enjoy the technical side, the jump is natural.\n**Study now:** [The Data Engineer roadmap](#/page/roadmap-data-engineer)\n\n<div class=\"callout callout-tip\"><span class=\"cfor\"><\/span><div>Analyst is the fastest role to land from zero, and the SQL you learn here is the same SQL engineers use. Many people start as an analyst and grow into engineering.<\/div><\/div>\n\n> **Next:** [compare all roles](#/page/role-comparison-table) · [Interview Bank](#/interview).\n"});
